{"id":"bp06","name":"Spiral Shelf Numbering","lang":"python","entry":"solution","params":["size"],"limit_s":4,"ordered":true,"desc":"<p>A storage room has <code>size</code> rows of <code>size</code> shelves. The robot numbers the shelves <code>1, 2, 3, ...</code> along a <b>clockwise spiral</b>: it starts at the top-left shelf, goes right along the first row, then down the last column, left along the last row, up the first column, and continues inwards.</p>\n<p>Your task is to return the grid of numbers as a list of rows. For <code>size = 0</code>, return an empty list.</p>\n<h4>Example</h4><p>For <code>size = 3</code>, the output should be</p><pre class=\"exv\">[[1, 2, 3], [8, 9, 4], [7, 6, 5]]</pre><div class=\"lim\"><b>[execution time limit]</b> 4 seconds (py3)<br><b>[memory limit]</b> 1 GB<br><b>[input]</b> integer size<br><b>[output]</b> array.array.integer</div>","starter":"def solution(size):\n    # write your code here\n    return []\n","hints":["Garde une direction (droite, bas, gauche, haut) et tourne quand la case suivante sort de la grille ou est déjà remplie.","size = 0 donne une liste vide."],"summary_fr":"Remplir une grille size x size avec 1, 2, 3... en spirale dans le sens des aiguilles d'une montre, en partant du coin en haut à gauche.","tags":["grille","directions","simulation"],"minutes":15,"source":"exercism/problem-specifications (MIT) · spiral-matrix","files":null,"visible":[{"input":{"size":3},"expected":{"value":[[1,2,3],[8,9,4],[7,6,5]]}},{"input":{"size":5},"expected":{"value":[[1,2,3,4,5],[16,17,18,19,6],[15,24,25,20,7],[14,23,22,21,8],[13,12,11,10,9]]}}],"hidden_n":8,"hidden":"","solution":""}